  "title": "International Women's Day Protests, Petrograd 1917",
  "summary": "On International Women's Day, 23 February 1917 in Russia (8 March elsewhere), women textile workers from the Vyborg district of Petrograd went on strike and marched toward the city centre demanding bread, joined by housewives. The protest quickly drew in other workers, and by the next day more than 200,000 workers were on strike.",
